      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstatic constexpr long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nstatic long long mod_pow(long long base, long long exp) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = result * base % MOD;\n        base = base * base % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<pair<int, int>> blocked;\n    blocked.reserve(m);\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        int y, x;\n        cin >> y >> x;\n        blocked.emplace_back(y, x);\n    }\n    sort(blocked.begin(), blocked.end());\n    blocked.erase(unique(blocked.begin(), blocked.end()), blocked.end());\n\n    if (binary_search(blocked.begin(), blocked.end(), make_pair(0, 0)) ||\n        binary_search(blocked.begin(), blocked.end(), make_pair(n - 1, n - 1))) {\n        cout << 0 << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const int max_steps = 2 * (n - 1);\n    vector<long long> fact(max_steps + 1), inv_fact(max_steps + 1);\n    fact[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= max_steps; ++i) fact[i] = fact[i - 1] * i % MOD;\n    inv_fact[max_steps] = mod_pow(fact[max_steps], MOD - 2);\n    for (int i = max_steps; i > 0; --i) inv_fact[i - 1] = inv_fact[i] * i % MOD;\n\n    auto choose = [&](int total, int taken) -> long long {\n        if (taken < 0 || taken > total) return 0;\n        return fact[total] * inv_fact[taken] % MOD * inv_fact[total - taken] % MOD;\n    };\n\n    vector<long long> ways(blocked.size());\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < blocked.size(); ++i) {\n        const int y = blocked[i].first;\n        const int x = blocked[i].second;\n        long long count = choose(y + x, y);\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < i; ++j) {\n            const int py = blocked[j].first;\n            const int px = blocked[j].second;\n            if (py <= y && px <= x) {\n                long long paths = choose((y - py) + (x - px), y - py);\n                count = (count - ways[j] * paths % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        ways[i] = count;\n    }\n\n    long long answer = choose(max_steps, n - 1);\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < blocked.size(); ++i) {\n        const int y = blocked[i].first;\n        const int x = blocked[i].second;\n        if (y <= n - 1 && x <= n - 1) {\n            long long paths = choose((n - 1 - y) + (n - 1 - x), n - 1 - y);\n            answer = (answer - ways[i] * paths % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << answer << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing the O(N²) column-dependent dynamic program with obstacle-ordered combinatorial inclusion-exclusion removes the serial row recurrence and reduces work to O(M² + N), which should help when obstacles are sparse.",
  "notes": "Counts monotone paths modulo 1e9+7 using factorial binomial coefficients and deduplicated blocked coordinates. No execution or validation was performed.",
